## 6. Run the Pipeline Directly (CLI)

You can also run the pipeline as a one-off CLI command without the test harness:

```powershell
# From repo root — add src/ to PYTHONPATH first
$env:PYTHONPATH = "src"
python -m pipeline.graph --pdf "src/scraper/data/raw/MAYBANK/MAYBANK_2024_Q3.pdf"

# Save output to JSON
python -m pipeline.graph --pdf "src/scraper/data/raw/MAYBANK/MAYBANK_2024_Q3.pdf" --output output.json
```

---

## 7. Quick Start Summary (Ordered Steps)

```powershell
# 1. Install pipeline deps
pip install -r src/pipeline/requirements.txt

# 2. (If running scraper) Install scraper deps + browsers
pip install -r src/scraper/requirements.txt
python -m playwright install chromium

# 3. Get a PDF (choose one):
#    a) Run scraper: python src/scraper/main.py
#    b) Drop PDF manually into src/scraper/data/raw/TICKER/TICKER_YEAR_PERIOD.pdf

# 4. Run smoke tests (no PDF/DB needed)
python tests/test_pipeline.py --smoke

# 5. Run full integration test (needs PDF + live keys + Supabase)
python tests/test_pipeline.py --integration --pdf "src/scraper/data/raw/MAYBANK/MAYBANK_2024_Q3.pdf"
```

